  <title>2.5.2: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00443</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.5.2: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1e2d5c34-6bc5-43ff-b9a0-4577173e16f0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>At a toy store, a family bought 3 toy cars, \(c\), and 2 teddy bears, \(b\), for
    $46. Later that month, another family bought 7 of the same toy cars, \(c\), and 2
    of the same teddy bears, \(b\), for $70. The system represents the situation:</para>
<para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3c+2b=46\\\;7c+2b=70\end{array}\right.\)</para>
<para>Which statement must be true?</para></section>
</content>
</document>
